    "created_at": "2021-10-05T14:30:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-05T14:30:57Z",
    "body": "Yes, I think this is a pretty tricky design space. Something that was entirely in the content area, like the dialog element, would avoid the problems of the existing methods. But then, shouldn't such content area alerts manifest in the DOM, like everything else in the content area? Maybe it should just be a wrapper around the dialog element?\r\n\r\nI like the general idea and I think it would make developers happy, but it needs a lot of design work; it's not just a matter of making the existing spec async.\r\n\r\nA library based on dialog might be a good first step.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
